      "sharedValueReasons": [],
      "rationale": "A muted terracotta core could give Mimic warmth while pale work surfaces keep structural comparisons readable. Brand warmth, recommendation emphasis, and operational status use separate roles.",
      "fit": "Fits if a welcoming tone should remain perceptible throughout sustained review.",
      "countercondition": "Reconsider if warm surfaces distract from comparing structure or make blocker emphasis difficult to distinguish.",
      "tradeoff": "Persistent warmth gives the workspace character but consumes more visual attention than an almost neutral canvas.",
      "screenDescriptions": {
        "proposal comparison": "On the warm background, three equal pale cards show Resume Board, Criteria Comparison Studio, and Run Timeline Investigation View for the local monitor redesign. Dark primary text names each direction. A pale selection strip marks Criteria Comparison Studio with the explicit label 'Proposed recommendation — not human-approved'; it is not a success badge.",
        "run in progress": "The current Mimic Run remains on a pale work surface with dark primary text and a muted blue 'Run in progress' icon and label. The three directions, proposed recommendation, pending blocker, and next action remain visible. No percentage or event timestamp appears.",
        "blocked work": "A pale blocker panel uses a brown-orange icon, border accent, and 'Pending blocker' label with dark primary text. The next action reads 'Review the pending blocker.' Criteria Comparison Studio retains its proposed-only label.",
        "selected proposal": "The proposed-selection detail uses the pale terracotta selection field behind Criteria Comparison Studio. Dark primary text explicitly says 'Proposed recommendation — not human-approved.' A dark warm action button labeled 'Review pending blocker' uses surface.raised text; its color does not imply approval.",
        "completed work": "Completed-work entries, if present, use green check icons and 'Complete' labels with dark primary text. The current Run still reads 'In progress,' the blocker remains pending, and Criteria Comparison Studio remains proposed only. Completion styling never implies approval of the recommendation."
      },
      "sourceObservations": "Observed mechanisms supplied by the user: case:kintone-color connects core yellow to Warm Smart and tests subordinate support colors and pairings; case:smarthr-color-roles separates semantic color responsibilities. Neither source establishes a Mimic palette or outcome.",
      "mimicPredictions": "The terracotta core, quiet warm surfaces, and separate recommendation and status colors are provisional Mimic predictions. Their usefulness for comparison and blocker recognition has not been tested. No source yellow or token values are copied."
    },
