      "sharedValueReasons": [],
      "rationale": "A neutral workspace could reserve violet for a small Mimic identity mark and the Run overview heading. Operational actions and statuses receive their own colors, keeping signature moments scarce.",
      "fit": "Fits if Mimic should feel recognizable at entry and overview moments while comparison remains visually restrained.",
      "countercondition": "Reconsider if identity needs to remain strongly visible throughout every working state.",
      "tradeoff": "Sparse signature use preserves attention for work but may make detailed screens feel less recognizably Mimic.",
      "screenDescriptions": {
        "proposal comparison": "A cool neutral background holds three equal white cards for Resume Board, Criteria Comparison Studio, and Run Timeline Investigation View for the local monitor redesign. Dark primary text carries the comparison. A pale violet selection strip labels Criteria Comparison Studio 'Proposed recommendation — not human-approved.' Saturated violet appears only in the small Mimic mark.",
        "run in progress": "The current Mimic Run uses a white surface, dark primary text, and a teal 'Run in progress' icon and label. A short violet accent appears at the Run overview heading, without filling the work panels. The same directions, proposed recommendation, pending blocker, and next action remain visible; no percentage or event timestamp appears.",
        "blocked work": "A white panel gives the pending blocker an ochre icon, border accent, and 'Pending blocker' label. Dark primary text states the next action: 'Review the pending blocker.' Brand violet remains confined to the identity mark, and Criteria Comparison Studio stays proposed only.",
        "selected proposal": "Criteria Comparison Studio appears on the pale violet selection field with dark primary text stating 'Proposed recommendation — not human-approved.' A slate-blue 'Review pending blocker' button uses surface text. Neither the signature accent nor the button acts as an approval indicator.",
        "completed work": "Completed-work entries, if present, receive green check icons and 'Complete' labels alongside dark primary text. There is no saturated brand celebration. The current Run stays in progress, the blocker stays pending, and Criteria Comparison Studio stays proposed only."
      },
      "sourceObservations": "Observed mechanisms supplied by the user: case:youtube-hue adjusts recognizable red and limits strong color to signature moments; case:smarthr-color-roles distinguishes semantic roles. YouTube's legacy-recognition rationale does not transfer directly because Mimic has no legacy red.",
      "mimicPredictions": "A new violet signature and its placement at identity and overview moments are provisional Mimic predictions. Reduced competition with work content is an untested expectation, not a research finding. No YouTube red or source token values are copied."
    },
