      "countercondition": "Reconsider if the interface remains flat and simple enough that surface nesting adds unnecessary complexity.",
      "tradeoff": "Layering provides spatial organization but requires consistent containment rules and can add visual weight.",
      "screenDescriptions": {
        "proposal comparison": "The gray workspace background contains a light comparison surface with three equal white raised cards: Resume Board, Criteria Comparison Studio, and Run Timeline Investigation View for the local monitor redesign. Dark primary text names each direction. A blue-gray selection strip marks Criteria Comparison Studio 'Proposed recommendation — not human-approved.'",
        "run in progress": "The current Mimic Run sits on the light work surface; white raised regions contain its details. Dark primary text and a muted blue 'Run in progress' icon and label establish status. The same directions, proposed recommendation, pending blocker, and next action remain visible. No percentage or event timestamp appears.",
        "blocked work": "A white raised blocker region inside the light work panel uses a muted brown icon, border accent, and 'Pending blocker' label. Dark primary text gives the next action: 'Review the pending blocker.' The surrounding hierarchy stays neutral, and Criteria Comparison Studio remains proposed only.",
